  "lean": {
    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1} [inst : MeasurableSpace E] [inst_1 : NormedAddCommGroup E] [inst_2 : InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n  [inst_3 : FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [BorelSpace E] {V : E → ℝ} (κ : NNReal),\n  1 ≤ κ →\n    ContDiff ℝ 2 V →\n      (∀ (x w : E), (↑κ)⁻¹ * ‖w‖ ^ 2 ≤ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x) w) w ∧ ((fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x) w) w ≤ ‖w‖ ^ 2) →\n        0 < Module.finrank ℝ E →\n          ∀ (η : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E) → ℝ),\n            Measurable η →\n              ∀ (c q Δ : ℝ),\n                0 < c →\n                  c < 1 / 4 →\n                    (∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)), 0 < η s ∧ η s ≤ c) →\n                      2 ≤ q →\n                        0 < Δ →\n                          Δ ≤ 1 / 2 →\n                            ∀ (s0 : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E))\n                              (M : ProbabilityTheory.Kernel (NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)) E)\n                              [ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel M],\n                              have d := ↑(Module.finrank ℝ E);\n                              have K := fun r => (1 + r) / ((↑κ)⁻¹ + r);\n                              have τ := fun s => if 2 ≤ K ↑s.1 then K ↑s.1 else c;\n                              have L := q + Real.log (K ↑s0.1 * d * q / Δ);\n                              have B := 1 / 1024 / (√(d * L) + L);\n                              have J := ⌈8 * Real.log (Real.exp 1 * K ↑s0.1 / B)⌉₊;\n                              have eps := Δ / √(↑J + 1);\n                              have v := fun s => (η s + τ s) / (1 + ↑s.1);\n                              have bp := fun s => s.1 + (v s)⁻¹.toNNReal;\n                              have obs := fun p => p.2.1 + √(τ p.1 / (1 + ↑p.1.1)) • p.2.2;\n                              have center := fun p => (↑(bp p.1))⁻¹ • (↑p.1.1 • p.1.2.1 + (v p.1)⁻¹ • obs p);\n                              have F := fun p x => V x + ↑(bp p.1) / 2 * ‖x - center p‖ ^ 2;\n                              have T := fun p x => x - (1 + ↑(bp p.1))⁻¹ • gradient (F p) x;\n                              have Qn := fun n p => ‖gradient (F p) ((T p)^[n] p.2.1)‖ ^ 2;\n                              have N := fun s =>\n                                if h : ∃ n, Qn n s ≤ (fun p => ((↑κ)⁻¹ + ↑(bp p.1)) * d) s then Nat.find h else 0;\n                              have update := fun p =>\n                                (bp p.1, center p, (T p)^[N p] p.2.1, p.1.2.2.2.1 + 1, fun n =>\n                                  Nat.casesOn n (obs p) p.1.2.2.2.2);\n                              have bb := fun s => Max.max (↑s.1) B⁻¹;\n                              have TF := fun s x => V x + bb s / 2 * ‖x - s.2.1‖ ^ 2;\n                              have TT := fun s x => x - (1 + bb s)⁻¹ • gradient (TF s) x;\n                              have TQn := fun n s => ‖gradient (TF s) ((TT s)^[n] s.2.2.1)‖ ^ 2;\n                              have TN := fun s => if h : ∃ n, TQn n s ≤ (fun s => d * bb s) s then Nat.find h else 0;\n                              have txp := fun s => (TT s)^[TN s] s.2.2.1;\n                              have TA := fun s => (bb s)⁻¹;\n                              have tg := fun s => gradient V (txp s);\n                              have th := fun s => s.2.1 - TA s • tg s;\n                              have tnu :=\n                                (MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.restrict (Set.Ioc 0 1)).prod\n                                  (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E);\n                              have tW := fun s p =>\n                                Min.min 1\n                                  (Max.max (-1)\n                                    (have s_1 := ((s, p.1), p.2).1.1;\n                                    have x := ((s, p.1), p.2).1.2;\n                                    have t := ((s, p.1), p.2).2.1;\n                                    have z := √(TA s_1) • ((s, p.1), p.2).2.2;\n                                    Inner.inner ℝ\n                                      ((Real.pi / 2) •\n                                        (Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * t) • (x - th s_1) - Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * t) • z))\n                                      (tg s_1 -\n                                        gradient V\n                                          (th s_1 + Real.sin (Real.pi / 2 * t) • (x - th s_1) +\n                                            Real.cos (Real.pi / 2 * t) • z))));\n                              have tproposal := fun s =>\n                                MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => th s + √(TA s) • z)\n                                  (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E);\n                              have trho := fun s =>\n                                MeasureTheory.Measure.infinitePi fun x =>\n                                  (tproposal s).prod\n                                    ((ProbabilityTheory.poissonMeasure\n                                          ⟨2 * 1,\n                                            le_of_lt\n                                              (mul_pos\n                                                (Mathlib.Meta.Positivity.pos_of_isNat\n                                                  (Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.isNat_ofNat ℝ (Eq.refl 2))\n                                                  (Eq.refl (Nat.ble 1 2)))\n                                                (Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.isNat_lt_true\n                                                  (Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.isNat_ofNat ℝ Nat.cast_zero)\n                                                  (Mathlib.Meta.NormNum.isNat_ofNat ℝ Nat.cast_one)\n                                                  (Eq.refl Bool.false)))⟩).prod\n                                      ((MeasureTheory.Measure.infinitePi fun x => tnu).prod\n                                        (MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace.volume.restrict (Set.Icc 0 1))));\n                              have tpi := fun s =>\n                                (MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => s.2.1 + √(TA s) • z)\n                                      (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E)).tilted\n                                  fun x => -V x;\n                              0 < B ∧\n                                0 < eps ∧\n                                  eps ≤ 1 / 2 ∧\n                                    (∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)), B⁻¹ ≤ ↑s.1 → bb s = ↑s.1) ∧\n                                      Measurable TN ∧\n                                        Measurable txp ∧\n                                          (∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                              TQn (TN s) s ≤ d * bb s ∧\n                                                (∀ j < TN s, d * bb s < TQn j s) ∧ ‖th s - txp s‖ ≤ √(d * TA s)) ∧\n                                            ∃ Lt P,\n                                              ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel Lt ∧\n                                                ProbabilityTheory.IsMarkovKernel P ∧\n                                                  (∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                                      P s =\n                                                        if B⁻¹ ≤ ↑s.1 then MeasureTheory.Measure.dirac s\n                                                        else\n                                                          MeasureTheory.Measure.map (fun z => update (s, z))\n                                                            ((M s).prod (ProbabilityTheory.stdGaussian E))) ∧\n                                                    ((P ^ J) s0) {s | B⁻¹ ≤ ↑s.1} = 1 ∧\n                                                      (∀ (m : ℕ), (Lt.comp (P ^ (J + m))) s0 = (Lt.comp (P ^ J)) s0) ∧\n                                                        ∀ (s : NNReal × E × E × ℕ × (ℕ → E)),\n                                                          ((Measurable fun omega =>\n                                                                if h :\n                                                                    ∃ n,\n                                                                      omega n ∈\n                                                                        {p |\n                                                                          p.2.2.2 ≤\n                                                                            ∏ i,\n                                                                              (1 + tW s (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) /\n                                                                                (2 * 1)} then\n                                                                  (omega (Nat.find h)).1\n                                                                else 0) ∧\n                                                              MeasureTheory.Measure.map\n                                                                    (fun omega =>\n                                                                      if h :\n                                                                          ∃ n,\n                                                                            omega n ∈\n                                                                              {p |\n                                                                                p.2.2.2 ≤\n                                                                                  ∏ i,\n                                                                                    (1 + tW s (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) /\n                                                                                      (2 * 1)} then\n                                                                        (omega (Nat.find h)).1\n                                                                      else 0)\n                                                                    (trho s) =\n                                                                  Lt s ∧\n                                                                (trho s)\n                                                                      {ω |\n                                                                        ∀ (n : ℕ),\n                                                                          ω n ∉\n                                                                            {p |\n                                                                              p.2.2.2 ≤\n                                                                                ∏ i,\n                                                                                  (1 + tW s (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) /\n                                                                                    (2 * 1)}} =\n                                                                    0 ∧\n                                                                  ∫⁻ (ω : ℕ → E × ℕ × (ℕ → ℝ × E) × ℝ),\n                                                                      1 +\n                                                                        ∑' (n : ℕ),\n                                                                          if\n                                                                              ∀ i < n,\n                                                                                ω i ∉\n                                                                                  {p |\n                                                                                    p.2.2.2 ≤\n                                                                                      ∏ i,\n                                                                                        (1 + tW s (p.1, p.2.2.1 ↑i)) /\n                                                                                          (2 * 1)} then\n                                                                            ↑(ω n).2.1\n                                                                          else 0 ∂trho s ≤\n                                                                    ENNReal.ofReal (1 + 2 * Real.exp 2)) ∧\n                                                            MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure (tpi s) ∧\n                                                              (tpi s).AbsolutelyContinuous (Lt s) ∧\n                                                                (Lt s).AbsolutelyContinuous (tpi s) ∧\n                                                                  MeasureTheory.Integrable\n                                                                      (fun x => ((tpi s).rnDeriv (Lt s) x).toReal ^ q)\n                                                                      (Lt s) ∧\n                                                                    MeasureTheory.Integrable\n                                                                        (fun x => ((Lt s).rnDeriv (tpi s) x).toReal ^ q)\n                                                                        (tpi s) ∧\n                                                                      0 <\n                                                                          ∫ (x : E),\n                                                                            ((tpi s).rnDeriv (Lt s) x).toReal ^\n                                                                              q ∂Lt s ∧\n                                                                        0 <\n                                                                            ∫ (x : E),\n                                                                              ((Lt s).rnDeriv (tpi s) x).toReal ^\n                                                                                q ∂tpi s ∧\n                                                                          ∫ (x : E),\n                                                                                ((tpi s).rnDeriv (Lt s) x).toReal ^\n                                                                                  q ∂Lt s ≤\n                                                                              1 + eps ^ 2 ∧\n                                                                            ∫ (x : E),\n                                                                                  ((Lt s).rnDeriv (tpi s) x).toReal ^\n                                                                                    q ∂tpi s ≤\n                                                                                1 + eps ^ 2 ∧\n                                                                              Real.log\n                                                                                      (∫ (x : E),\n                                                                                        ((tpi s).rnDeriv (Lt s)\n                                                                                              x).toReal ^\n                                                                                          q ∂Lt s) /\n                                                                                    (q - 1) ≤\n                                                                                  eps ^ 2 ∧\n                                                                                Real.log\n                                                                                      (∫ (x : E),\n                                                                                        ((Lt s).rnDeriv (tpi s)\n                                                                                              x).toReal ^\n                                                                                          q ∂tpi s) /\n                                                                                    (q - 1) ≤\n                                                                                  eps ^ 2",
    "statement_sha256": "fec9ed0bd1777b77c64f297ed7a09967f1a2094cede1eb251059464c60add721",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "NNReal denotes nonnegative reals; upward arrows are real coercions. Module.finrank is real vector-space dimension. ContDiff R 2 is C2 regularity. fderiv and gradient are genuine Frechet and inner-product derivatives in the displayed spatial argument.",
      "Kernel S X is a measurable family of measures on X indexed by S; IsMarkovKernel means every fiber is a probability. Measure.map is pushforward. Measure.prod is product measure. Measure.infinitePi is the countable product measure with the given coordinate laws. Nested products associate right.",
      "stdGaussian E is the centered Gaussian probability with identity covariance. volume is canonical real volume. volume.restrict(Ioc 0 1) is Lebesgue measure restricted to(0,1]; Icc 0 1 is[0,1]. poissonMeasure of a nonnegative real is the Poisson probability with that mean. A Fin n index runs from0 to n-1, with empty product equal to1 when n=0. Every displayed acceptance product is indexed by Fin of that attempt batch-size coordinate, even when the pretty-printer only displays the product index name.",
      "A measure tilted f is exponential tilting by exp(f), normalized using the integral and Mathlib total-inverse conventions. This is a definition of a measure, not an implicit integrability premise. mu.rnDeriv nu is the extended nonnegative Radon-Nikodym derivative of mu with respect to nu; toReal is the standard real conversion, with infinity sent to0. The notation mu absolutelyContinuous nu means every nu-null measurable set is mu-null.",
      "ENNReal is the extended nonnegative reals. ENNReal.ofReal(r)=max(r,0). The integral with superscript minus is nonnegative extended integration. Integrable denotes Bochner integrability, including almost-everywhere strong measurability and finite norm integral. An ordinary integral uses Mathlib total Bochner conventions. Equality with superscript m relative to a measure means almost-everywhere equality. A tsum is a countable sum.",
      "Function iteration T^[n] includes identity at n=0. Nat.find takes the least natural satisfying the supplied existential witness. A dependent if may use that witness in its selected branch. A displayed have inside a type is a local let binding. Real inverse,division,sqrt and logarithm are total functions under Mathlib conventions. The context explains notation only and does not supply source identity, additional hypotheses or extra conclusions.",
      "Kernel composition Lt composed with P means first draw the intermediate state from P and then the output from Lt. Kernel powers are repeated composition, with power zero the identity kernel. Nat.ceil is the least natural at least its real argument. Nat.casesOn applied to an index defines a sequence by its zeroth value and shifted tail. The displayed acceptance product is indexed by Fin of the displayed batch size, including empty product one at batch size zero."
    ]
